    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d313">

                <pb facs="0424" n="336" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg336"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-08-03"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 3,
                    1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Choate reports that Lord Lansdowne desires to know the views of the United
                    States Government on the sinking of the <hi rendition="#italic">Knight
                        Commander</hi> and the depredations of the volunteer fleet on neutrals, and
                    generally concerning the dealings of belligerents with neutrals to enforce the
                    right of search for contraband.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
